 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 3.2,
   "end": 6.377,
   "text": "One Sabbath, they walked through the grain fields.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 7.977,
   "end": 9.923,
   "text": "Look. They are breaking the Sabbath.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 10.823,
   "end": 14.574,
   "text": "The Sabbath was made for people. Not people for the Sabbath.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 16.174,
   "end": 20.154,
   "text": "Later, in the synagogue, a man sat with a withered hand.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 21.154,
   "end": 24.557,
   "text": "And they watched. Waiting for him to break the rule.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 25.757,
   "end": 27.467,
   "text": "Stand up. Come to the middle.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 28.467,
   "end": 33.764,
   "text": "Is it right on the Sabbath to do good, or to do evil? To save a life, or to kill?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 34.364,
   "end": 35.406,
   "text": "Silence.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 37.006,
   "end": 38.453,
   "text": "Stretch out your hand.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 40.253,
   "end": 42.043,
   "text": "And it was made whole.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 43.843,
   "end": 47.272,
   "text": "That night, they went out into the dark, and made a plan.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 47.872,
   "end": 49.345,
   "text": "He has to die.",
   "tempter": true
  },
  {
   "start": 51.145,
   "end": 54.442,
   "text": "Follow for part five.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}